# Error Documentation

## Part A — Portfolio (this project)

### A1. Node 16 has no stable `node:test`

- **Context**: `node --version` is v16.16.0; `node:test` landed in 16.17/18.
- **Symptom**: `node --test` fails with `bad option: --test`.
- **Resolution**: Shared assert-based harness at `test/lib/test-runner.js`, suites run
  through `test/run-all.js` (`npm test`), which exits non-zero on any failure.
- **State**: Resolved. Revisit only if the toolchain moves to Node 18+.

### A2. UMD module depending on another UMD module

- **Context**: `utils/project-data.js` needs `resume-data.js` for role provenance.
- **Symptom**: Reaching for `globalThis` inside the factory argument list resolves
  the wrong `this` and yields `undefined` in the browser.
- **Resolution**: Pass the dependency in from the wrapper body, choosing
  `require('./resume-data.js')` under CommonJS and `root.ResumeData` in the browser.
  In HTML, load `resume-data.js` **before** `project-data.js`.
- **State**: Resolved. Apply the same shape to any future cross-module util.

### A3. JS-dependent CSS can blank the page for no-JS visitors

- **Context**: `.pf-reveal` starts at `opacity: 0` for the scroll animation, and the
  mobile nav list is hidden when collapsed.
- **Symptom**: With JavaScript disabled, hidden content would never be revealed.
- **Resolution**: `theme-init.js` adds `.pf-js` to `<html>`, and every hiding rule is
  scoped under `.pf-js`. No JS means nothing is hidden.
- **State**: Resolved. Never write a hiding rule that is not gated by `.pf-js`.

### A4. Filtered items never fade in

- **Context**: Filter chips toggle `hidden` on cards that also carry `.pf-reveal`.
- **Symptom**: An item hidden before its IntersectionObserver callback fires stays at
  `opacity: 0` after being un-hidden, so it appears blank.
- **Resolution**: `experience.js` and `projects.js` add `is-visible` to every item
  when a filter is applied, independent of the observer.
- **State**: Resolved.

### A5. Duplicated header and footer markup across six pages

- **Context**: No build step, so the nav block is repeated in every page.
- **Symptom**: Editing the nav in five of six pages is silent and easy to miss.
- **Resolution**: `test/page-markup.test.js` asserts every page contains every
  `NAV_LINKS` entry with the exact `data-nav-key` and `href`, and that no internal
  link 404s. Drift now fails the build instead of shipping.
- **State**: Mitigated. Extracting a partial is a P3 item in `tasks/tasks_plan.md`.

### A6. Root-absolute paths do not work over `file://`

- **Context**: All references use `/pages/...`, `/utils/...`, `/media/...`.
- **Symptom**: Opening `index.html` by double-clicking renders unstyled HTML.
- **Resolution**: Always preview through a server from the repository root
  (`npm start` or `python3 -m http.server`). Documented in `README.md`.
- **State**: Expected behaviour, not a bug — but it surprises people, so it is noted.

### A7. No linting for a zero-build project

- **Context**: A stray newline inside a `.pf-visually-hidden` declaration produced an
  invalid property that no tool flagged.
- **Symptom**: Silently dropped CSS rule.
- **Resolution**: Caught by review. An HTML/CSS validator step in `npm test` is a P3
  backlog item; until then, changed CSS gets read back before commit.
- **State**: Open (low severity, backlog item).

## Part B — Inherited from the sibling `PersonalWebsite` project

Kept because the lessons still apply to any static site in this workspace.

### B1. Audio file with a space in its name fails to load

- **Resolution**: Kebab-case media filenames; `%20` encoding if a space is unavoidable.

### B2. Sticky mini-player covers the footer

- **Resolution**: Add body padding while the player is expanded; collapse to a corner
  chip when minimised.

### B3. Uneven card heights in media grids

- **Resolution**: Grid `align-items: stretch`, cards `height: 100%` with
  `display: flex; flex-direction: column`, media region `flex: 1`.

### B4. Tailwind body utilities hide a shared background image

- **Resolution**: Keep the backdrop only in `theme.css`; never put `bg-*` utilities
  on `<body>`. (Not applicable here — this project ships no Tailwind.)
